            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment by fecal microbiota transplantation for Japanese patients with refractory Clostridium difficile infection: A prospective case series.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1684-1182(17)30235-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jmii.2017.08.027</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We prospectively enrolled four Japanese patients with refractory Clostridium difficile infection (CDI) and were treated with a single fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT). The average age of the patients was 83.7 years. All patients had a successful clinical course for up to 3 months without any adverse events.</AbstractText>
